            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Foot patrol allows you to not be distracted by the operation of the vehicle and the mental processes required for safe and proper driving. From a vehicle, it is more difficult to hear the sound of a window breaking, or to notice the smell of smoke. Conducting your patrol on foot allows you to use all of your senses, and makes it easier for you to stay close to the persons or property you are tasked with protecting. When on foot, you are able to access secluded areas, such as stairwells, and you have more opportunity to interact with the people you may be helping protect. Having a chance to chat or find out about things that are going on helps you to be more aware of the setting and even more aware of when things aren’t quite right."
